---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="The backend decides how fast people can be let in. Everything else, such as the wait and the polling traffic, follows from that and from the size of the crowd.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Fans who want in (thousands) <input type="range" min="100" max="5000" step="100" value="1000" data-f /> <b data-fval></b></label>
      <label>Share arriving in the first minute (%) <input type="range" min="10" max="90" step="5" value="60" data-s /> <b data-sval></b></label>
      <label>Shoppers the backend can hold at once <input type="range" min="2000" max="100000" step="2000" value="20000" data-c /> <b data-cval></b></label>
      <label>Seconds a shopper keeps a slot <input type="range" min="60" max="600" step="30" value="240" data-h /> <b data-hval></b></label>
      <label>Waiting page checks its place every (s) <input type="range" min="5" max="60" step="5" value="10" data-p /> <b data-pval></b></label>
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Assumptions: the crowd is already waiting when the shop opens, so everyone polls from the start. A slot is free again after the hold time, so the safe admission rate is slots divided by hold time (Little's law). A poll answer is about 600 bytes, there are 300 edge locations, a stored token takes about 100 bytes and a join-log entry about 24 bytes.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const val = (s: string) => Number(q<HTMLInputElement>(s).value);
    const rows = Array.from({ length: 10 }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const fmt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US');
    const bytes = (n: number) => (n >= 1e9 ? `${(n / 1e9).toFixed(1)} GB` : n >= 1e6 ? `${(n / 1e6).toFixed(1)} MB` : `${fmt(n / 1e3)} KB`);
    const span = (s: number) => (s >= 7200 ? `${(s / 3600).toFixed(1)} hours` : s >= 120 ? `${Math.round(s / 60)} minutes` : `${Math.round(s)} seconds`);
    function draw() {
      const fans = val('[data-f]') * 1000; const share = val('[data-s]') / 100; const slots = val('[data-c]'); const hold = val('[data-h]'); const poll = val('[data-p]');
      q('[data-fval]').textContent = fmt(fans / 1000) + 'k'; q('[data-sval]').textContent = String(share * 100);
      q('[data-cval]').textContent = fmt(slots); q('[data-hval]').textContent = String(hold); q('[data-pval]').textContent = String(poll);
      const arrivals = (fans * share) / 60; const rate = slots / hold; const polls = fans / poll;
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['Arrivals per second in the first minute', fmt(arrivals)],
        ['Safe admission rate (slots / hold time)', `${rate.toFixed(1)} per second`],
        ['Overload if nobody is held back', `${fmt(arrivals / rate)} times`],
        ['Time to let everyone in', span(fans / rate)],
        ['Median wait if all arrive at the start', span(fans / rate / 2)],
        ['Place checks per second from the waiting page', fmt(polls)],
        ['Bandwidth for those checks (600 bytes each)', `${bytes(polls * 600)} per second`],
        ['Origin fetches per second with a 1-second edge cache', fmt(300)],
        ['Queue state with signed tokens', `about 16 bytes, plus ${bytes(fans * 24)} of join log`],
        ['If every token were stored on the server', bytes(fans * 100)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
